    {
      "id": "probeharbor-probe",
      "name": "ProbeHarbor probe",
      "url": "https://esp32bench.dev/projects/probeharbor-probe",
      "level": "Starter",
      "minutes": 15,
      "tags": [
        "probeharbor",
        "sensors",
        "wireless"
      ],
      "summary": "Prebuilt sensor firmware from the ProbeHarbor project. Flash it from this page, then it finds a temperature sensor by itself and posts a reading every minute.",
      "firmware": "prebuilt",
      "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/doodersrage/probeharbor/tree/main/firmware/probeharbor-probe",
      "libraries": [],
      "baud": 115200,
      "needs": [
        [
          "ds18b20",
          "dht22",
          "i2c"
        ]
      ],
      "parts": [
        {
          "quantity": 1,
          "name": "ESP32 dev board",
          "link": "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08D5ZD528"
        },
        {
          "quantity": 1,
          "name": "or ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1",
          "link": "https://www.adafruit.com/product/5336"
        },
        {
          "quantity": 1,
          "name": "or ESP32-C3-DevKitM-1",
          "link": "https://www.adafruit.com/product/5337"
        },
        {
          "quantity": 1,
          "name": "DS18B20 waterproof probe, or a DHT22",
          "link": "https://www.adafruit.com/product/381"
        },
        {
          "quantity": 1,
          "name": "4.7 kΩ resistor, pull-up for the probe data line",
          "link": "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08QRZRRGB"
        },
        {
          "quantity": 1,
          "name": "Optional I2C sensor: SHT31",
          "link": "https://www.adafruit.com/product/2857"
        },
        {
          "quantity": 1,
          "name": "Optional I2C sensor: BME280",
          "link": "https://www.adafruit.com/product/2652"
        },
        {
          "quantity": 1,
          "name": "Optional I2C sensor: AHT20",
          "link": "https://www.adafruit.com/product/4566"
        },
        {
          "quantity": 1,
          "name": "Optional door reed switch",
          "link": "https://www.adafruit.com/product/375"
        },
        {
          "quantity": 2,
          "name": "Optional 100 kΩ resistors, battery divider",
          "link": "https://www.adafruit.com/product/2787"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Flashing writes a merged image at offset 0, which also erases saved Wi-Fi and the device key. Send settings again after every flash.",
        "From firmware 1.5.0 the probe updates itself from ProbeHarbor, installing only updates signed with ProbeHarbor's key, and goes back to the old version if the new one cannot post. You only need to flash it once.",
        "It also checks ProbeHarbor's certificate. If the check fails it prints TT tls: certificate not verified, keeps posting, and tries again a day later; ProbeHarbor's device page shows a warning meanwhile.",
        "Firmware before 1.5.1 could crash when settings arrived twice, which the form below does if the probe is slow to answer. A crash report naming WiFiManager::shutdownConfigPortal() is this; 1.5.1 and later are fixed.",
        "From firmware 1.5.1 a probe that crashed reports it once with its next reading, and ProbeHarbor's device page shows it under Last crash.",
        "The ESP32-C3 SuperMini often cannot join Wi-Fi at full transmit power. From 1.5.1 the probe retries at low power and keeps using it on that board; place it near the access point.",
        "TT post -5 means the reply was lost, not the reading. In testing the server had stored both readings that printed -5.",
        "An I2C sensor that is found at boot but then prints TT sensor problem usually has a loose power or ground wire. That was the cause when it happened on the S3.",
        "Hold BOOT for five seconds to erase Wi-Fi and the key. Feather boards have no button on GPIO 0, so resend settings instead.",
        "On a Feather, probe data on GPIO 4 is the pad marked A5 and the door input on GPIO 26 is A0."
      ],
      "open": [
        "Leak and battery inputs on any board",
        "Setup portal and the five-second BOOT reset on the ESP32 and S3",
        "DS18B20 on the S3 and C3, and any I2C sensor on the C3",
        "UART port on the S3 and on a C3 DevKitM-1",
        "A long unattended run on the S3"
      ],
      "verified": [
        {
          "board": "esp32",
          "what": "Browser flash, USB settings, Wi-Fi and first reading with a DS18B20",
          "when": "firmware 1.0.1"
        },
        {
          "board": "esp32",
          "what": "DHT22 on GPIO 4",
          "when": "firmware 1.1.1"
        },
        {
          "board": "esp32",
          "what": "BME280 on I2C: temperature, humidity and pressure",
          "when": "firmware 1.2.2"
        },
        {
          "board": "esp32",
          "what": "SHT31 on I2C",
          "when": "firmware 1.2.3"
        },
        {
          "board": "esp32",
